// QEMU reactive smoke — proves event injection -> at-watcher -> host-fn -> printf
//
// Goal: exercise the v0.7.1 reactive C-API end-to-end on QEMU.  The C side
// (reactive_smoke_main.c) registers `ping` (event with destructure) and
// `signal_pass` (host fn), injects 3 events with seq=1,2,3, and drives
// urbi_step until quiescent.
//
// Drift from spec §6.4: the original sketch used `cout << "got ping seq="
// << seq;` for an extra UART marker per event.  Two v0.7.1 lex gaps
// prevent that form:
//   * `cout << ...` is not tokenized — there's no stream-operator lex
//     rule.  See the eye_demo rewrite in commit 7fb0c23 for the same
//     drift; cite is tests/chk/stdlib/containers/list_core.chk:8-10 for
//     the broader "stdlib API beats sugar in v0.7.1" rule.
//   * Inline destructure `at (ping ?(seq)) { ... }` parses, but the
//     canonical idiom matching tests/chk/reactive/at/*.chk is the
//     callback form `at (ping?) function (seq) { ... }`.
//
// We drop the `cout` line — the `signal_pass(seq)` call still produces a
// per-event UART marker via C-side printf, which is what the
// expected_markers.txt oracle now greps for.  No urbi-side writer output
// in this smoke; the writer hook is still installed in case a future
// extension needs it.
at (ping?) function (seq) {
    signal_pass(seq);
};
